@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `yeaH`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 98% of them, at 0.15 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 52 to 89%, 69 persistent and 10 shell, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 82% of calls {S2}. A branch of 14 families runs through columns 1 to 14, a parallel path carried instead of the most carried families there, share 10 to 11% {S2.b1}. The `astC` to `astE` genes, columns 36 to 40, are [[succinylglutamate metabolism]] {S2.c36-40, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 92%, and hesitates less there, 0.15 against 0.29 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 8, `ydjL`, is a fork column, at 0.90 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends on variable columns.** Columns 64 to 78, `thrS` to `hemP`, are carried by 74 to 84%, all persistent {S2.c64-78}. The last column is `aroH`, in 63% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.29 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.22 against 0.16 bits, and names fewer genes, 66% against 96% {C}.

